.TH SDL_GetAudioStreamProperties 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetAudioStreamProperties \- Get the properties associated with an audio stream.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_PropertiesID SDL_GetAudioStreamProperties(SDL_AudioStream *stream);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The application can hang any data it wants here, but the following properties are understood by SDL:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_AUDIOSTREAM_AUTO_CLEANUP_BOOLEAN :
if true (the default), the stream be automatically cleaned up when the audio subsystem quits\[char46] If set to false, the streams will persist beyond that\[char46] This property is ignored for streams created through
.BR SDL_OpenAudioDeviceStream (),
and will always be cleaned up\[char46] Streams that are not cleaned up will still be unbound from devices when the audio subsystem quits\[char46] This property was added in SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I stream
the
.BR SDL_AudioStream
to query\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a valid property ID on success or 0 on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

